   "subject": "Regularization: ddexp alternative",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">Dear All,</span></div><div><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">I am trying the Bayesian Lasso ( beta j ~ DoubleExpo(0, sigma^2 ) where:  sigma<span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.66px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">^2 <span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.66px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\">~  InvGamma(0.01, 0.01).</span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.66px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.66px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.66px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.66px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"> I realized that &quot;ddexp&quot; (<span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(31,78,121);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">a\r\nLaplace double exponential prior in JAGS ) </span>is under development in NIMBLE. Is there an alternative distribution OR a different formulation to the following?</span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.66px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><span style=\"display:inline!important;float:none;background-color:transparent;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.66px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><br></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(31,73,125);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.66px;font-variant:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline!important;white-space:normal;float:none;background-color:transparent\"><span style=\"text-align:left;color:rgb(31,73,125);text-transform:none;text-indent:0px;letter-spacing:normal;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:14.66px;font-variant:normal;word-spacing:0px;display:inline!important;white-space:normal;float:none;background-color:transparent\"><div style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13.33px;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:100%;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.99px;overflow:visible;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><span><span>nimbleCode({</span></span></div><div style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13.33px;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:100%;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.99px;overflow:visible;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><span><span>  #... some previous code</span></span></div><div style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13.33px;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:100%;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.99px;overflow:visible;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><span><span> </span></span></div><div style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13.33px;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:100%;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.99px;overflow:visible;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><span><span><span> <font face=\"arial,sans-serif\"> <font color=\"#073763\"># Likelihood<br></font></font></span></span></span></div><div style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13.33px;font-size-adjust:none;font-stretch:100%;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:19.99px;overflow:visible;text-align:left;text-decoration:none;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><span><span><span><font color=\"#073763\"><font face=\"arial,sans-serif\">  for(i in 1:n){<br>    Y[i]   ~ dnorm(mu[i], inv.var)<br>    mu[i] &lt;- alpha + inprod(X[i,], beta[])<br>  }<br><br>  # Prior for beta<br>  for(j in 1:p){<br>    beta[j] ~ ddexp(0, inv.var.b)<br>  }<br><br>  # Prior for the inverse variance<br>  inv.var   ~ dgamma(0.01, 0.01)<br>  inv.var.b ~ dgamma(0.01, 0.01)<br><div>  alpha     ~ dnorm(0, 0.01)</div><div><br></div></font>\r\n</font><font color=\"#073763\"><span>#... some later code<font color=\"#004000\" face=\"&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;Helvetica&quot;,sans-serif\" size=\"2\"> })</font></span></font></span></span></span><span><span></span></span></div><div><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></div><div>All the best,</div><div>Mahdieh</div></span></span></span></div><div><b></b><i></i><u></u><sub></sub><sup></sup><strike></strike><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "YYNPEZ8GAwAJ",
   "from": "Chris Paciorek",
   "author": "5fa2a363d4ddd1d1",
   "date": "2018-09-07T14:49:39Z",
   "subject": "Re: Regularization: ddexp alternative",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Mahdieh,\r<br>\r<br>This is a case where you can use a user-defined distribution. Please\r<br>see Section 12.2 of the manual. Given that there is an example of\r<br>writing a simple exponential distribution there, hopefully it will be\r<br>straightforward for you to write the ddexp case.\r<br>\r<br>You could also, without having to define your own distribution, write\r<br>the double exponential as a scale mixture of normals using a parameter\r<br>augmentation approach, but this introduces additional parameters so\r<br>would likely decrease MCMC efficiency. So I&#39;d suggest the user-defined\r<br>distribution approach.\r<br>\r<br>Filling out some of the extra distributions that we have said we&#39;d\r<br>like to add always seems to take lower priority than other things\r<br>we&#39;re doing, but given your interest and that this case is a common\r<br>one, hopefully we can add this as part of NIMBLE in the next release\r<br>or two.\r<br>Chris\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "On Fri, Sep 7, 2018 at 3:26 AM &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">mahdieh...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Dear All,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I am trying the Bayesian Lasso ( beta j ~ DoubleExpo(0, sigma^2 ) where:  sigma^2 ~  InvGamma(0.01, 0.01).\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;  I realized that &quot;ddexp&quot; (a Laplace double exponential prior in JAGS ) is under development in NIMBLE. Is there an alternative distribution OR a different formulation to the following?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; nimbleCode({\r<br>&gt;   #... some previous code\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;   # Likelihood\r<br>&gt;   for(i in 1:n){\r<br>&gt;     Y[i]   ~ dnorm(mu[i], inv.var)\r<br>&gt;     mu[i] &lt;- alpha + inprod(X[i,], beta[])\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;   # Prior for beta\r<br>&gt;   for(j in 1:p){\r<br>&gt;     beta[j] ~ ddexp(0, inv.var.b)\r<br>&gt;   }\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;   # Prior for the inverse variance\r<br>&gt;   inv.var   ~ dgamma(0.01, 0.01)\r<br>&gt;   inv.var.b ~ dgamma(0.01, 0.01)\r<br>&gt;   alpha     ~ dnorm(0, 0.01)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; #... some later code })\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; All the best,\r<br>&gt; Mahdieh\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; --\r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;nimble-users&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nimble-users...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nimble...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; To view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/nimble-users/5ad36cb4-f651-4cbf-9b2c-2dad569f54ab%40googlegroups.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/nimble-users/5ad36cb4-f651-4cbf-9b2c-2dad569f54ab%2540googlegroups.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478624081000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QIlMbBYj4MMM7xycxkoEN\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/nimble-users/5ad36cb4-f651-4cbf-9b2c-2dad569f54ab%40googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792478624081000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0P9JTnbO5lw_IHtCNBwD6B\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
